# CONFIG HOOKS - run after the configuration changed
#
#        node.py, called after a node is created, changed, cloned or removed:
#        - postcreate(name, group)
#        - postupdate(name, group)
#        - rename(name, newname)
#        - delete(name)
#        - bulk(fullset)       the whole node and group set, from the housekeeper
#
#        group.py, the same for a group, with the member nodes instead of a group:
#        - postcreate(name, nodes)
#        - postupdate(name, nodes)
#        - rename(name, newname)
#        - delete(name)
#        - bulk(fullset)
#
#        interface.py, called after a node interface is created, changed, renamed or
#        removed. The node is what changed - its hostname and its scrape address are
#        derived from the interface it provisions over - so the node is what travels:
#        - postcreate(name, interface, macaddress, ipaddress, ipaddress_ipv6, network,
#                     networktype, zone)
#        - postupdate(name, interface, macaddress, ipaddress, ipaddress_ipv6, network,
#                     networktype, zone)
#                              networktype and zone are the network's, and are carried
#                              only where the change left the interface on the network it
#                              was already on
#        - rename(name, interface, newinterfacename)
#                              interface is the name it had; a rename moves no address
#        - delete(name, interface)
#        - macaddressupdate(name, interface, macaddress)
#                              where the macaddress moved and the addressing did not - a
#                              write that moves an address carries the macaddress in its
#                              own postupdate, because exactly one of these fires per
#                              interface. An extension point: shipped empty, because
#                              nothing downstream reads a macaddress
#                              BEWARE that a node writes its macaddress as it boots, and
#                              that write is journalled, so whatever is put in here is
#                              paid once per node per boot on both controllers. Anything
#                              slow or outward-facing there costs a cluster boot
#        no bulk: a whole-set operation is the node and group set, which node.py and
#        group.py already carry
#        BEWARE that only the interface a node provisions over has an address a controller
#        can reach - an IPoIB address, for one, is not - so an address from any other
#        interface must not be scraped. The node document from the API carries the node's
#        resolved provision_interface: compare it with the interface handed to you here
#
#        dns.py, called while the DNS zones are rendered:
#        - nsupdate(host, ipaddress, zone, ttl, key_name, key_secret, key_hmac)
#                              for a node that takes its address from a DHCP pool
#        - notify(master, slaves, key)
#
#        each returns <True|False>,"message"
#
# Loaded by name, plugins/hooks/config/node.py, group.py, interface.py and dns.py.
# No search path.
